            ],
            "instructions": [
                "Remove the two M4x5mm bolts on the back of the TV plate using a Phillips #00 screwdriver.",
                "Unplug the TV cables before removing the TV from the wall."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272929"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272942",
            "image_urls": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/Mw641cLcnbQGVljD.medium"
            ],
            "image_alt_text": [
                "Fix a Loose Mounting Dream MD2462 TV Wall Mount: step 2, image 1 of 3"
            ],
            "thumbnail_urls": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/Mw641cLcnbQGVljD.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/hMTsflCyafRpn4QY.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/VuDn2bf2NTFER1dL.200x150"
            ],
            "instructions": [
                "Remove the three lag bolts from the wall mount by using a 13mm open-end wrench.",
                "If it is too loose, it can just be pulled out."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272942"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272949",
            "instructions": [
                "Fill the holes where the screws were secured using drywall spackle."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272949"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272950",
            "instructions": [
                "Locate the wooden studs on the wall using a stud finder or knock on the wall to see if the stud is behind the wall."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272950"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272951",
            "instructions": [
                "Use a pencil to mark three holes on the wall.",
                "Use a 3/8-inch drill bit to drill three holes at the marked positions.",
                "Secure the wall mount into the wooden studs using new screws or bolts.",
                "Ensure that all the screws are firmly secured to the wooden stud."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272951"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272952",
            "instructions": [
                "Test the firmness of the TV wall mount by gently pushing it up and down."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272952"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 7,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272953",
            "instructions": [
                "Gently replace the TV back on the wall mount."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272953"
            }
        },
        {
            "step_number": 8,
            "title": "",
            "step_id": "s272954",
            "instructions": [
                "Make sure the TV is secure and well-centered on the wall mount using a spirit level gauge to confirm the inclination."
            ],
            "links": {
                "edit_step_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/137176/272954"
            }
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
